/* Airline Agent Policy — tau2-airline
 *
 * Source: experiments/translation/spec.md
 * Mode L (trace-grounded): every structural assumption below was read
 * off the 88 captured, oracle-labeled decision points in
 * outputs/variant-set/run5/scenarios.json and the trace-derived system
 * profile in outputs/variant-set/run5/system.md.
 *
 * Content checks are custom C++ functors in airline_functors.cpp
 * (keyword/phrase matchers). No @llm_check_fn, no ActionMetadata, no
 * ask-kind reasons: this deployment supplies none of them, and a rule
 * that depends on one would read as coverage while enforcing nothing.
 *
 * Round-trip audit: PASS (2026-08-20)
 */
#include "../../../../policies/common_policy.dl"

/* ── K-Constraints (verified against the run5 traces) ──────────────
   K1: Two agent names speak in every slice — "LLMAgent" (the airline
       assistant) and "UserSimulator" (the simulated customer). The
       capture records the SAME conversation twice with the roles
       flipped: all 326 messages with agent="UserSimulator",
       agent_role=user are verbatim copies of the assistant's own
       turns (checked: 326/326 matched an LLMAgent assistant message,
       0 unmatched). A rule keyed on agent_role=$UserRole() alone would
       therefore accept the agent's own proposal as the customer's
       consent. EVERY user-content rule below filters
       msg.agent = "LLMAgent" AND msg.agent_role = $UserRole().
   K2: Tool results are agent="LLMAgent", agent_role=agent
       ($AgentType()), and carry the payload as JSON in msg.contents;
       ToolResult(id, fn_name, args) marks the node.
   K3: Tool calls ride on agent="LLMAgent", agent_role=assistant
       messages whose contents are empty and whose tools_json holds the
       call. The gated call itself arrives as Actions(idx, ...), not as
       a graph node.
   K4: The conversation is linear: all 1609 LLMAgent nodes across the
       88 slices are DIRECT predecessors of the Current node carrying
       an EdgeData message_index (0..N), and exactly one edge per
       decision point carries proximal=1 — the immediately preceding
       turn (41 of 88 a user turn, 47 a tool result). The confirmation
       rule (C3) reads that single proximal edge.
   K5: get_reservation_details results carry cabin, created_at,
       insurance ("yes"/"no"), total_baggages, nonfree_baggages,
       passengers[] ({first_name,last_name,dob}) and flights[]
       ({flight_number,origin,destination,date,price}) at top level.
       book_reservation, cancel_reservation and update_reservation_*
       return the SAME reservation shape, so reservation state is read
       from ANY tool result carrying a reservation_id — keying on
       get_reservation_details alone would miss post-update state.
   K6: get_user_details results carry membership as a bare string and
       payment_methods as an OBJECT keyed by payment id (not an array)
       — hence @json_object_has_key(profile, "payment_methods", pid).
   K7: In these traces update_reservation_flights, calculate and
       search_* results are NOT JSON objects (bare arrays, numbers or
       "Error: ..." strings), and transfer_to_human_agents produced no
       result node at all (4 calls, 0 results). No rule joins on a
       transfer_to_human_agents result, and reservation state is only
       taken from payloads that actually expose a reservation_id.
   K8: One slice holds several states of the same reservation (before
       and after an update) — up to 3 for FQ8APE. "The reservation" is
       therefore the state with the highest message_index, never any
       matching state.
   ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */

/* ── Structured Spec ──────────────────────────────────────────────
   C1  Airline tool calls are authorized by default; every rule below
       is a carve-out. (spec: the agent books, modifies, cancels, and
       handles refunds/compensation)
   C2  A denied call is refused with an error the agent can read.
   C3  Writes to the booking database (book_reservation,
       update_reservation_flights / _passengers / _baggages,
       cancel_reservation) require explicit user confirmation as the
       immediately preceding turn.
   C4  get_user_details / book_reservation: the user id must have been
       provided by the user or returned by a tool, never invented.
   C5  book_reservation: at most five passengers.
   C6  book_reservation: every passenger's date of birth must appear
       in the conversation (user-provided or from a tool result).
   C7  book_reservation: at most one travel certificate, at most one
       credit card, at most three gift cards.
   C8  book_reservation / update_reservation_*: every payment id must
       exist in the user's profile payment_methods.
   C9  book_reservation / update_reservation_baggages: the paid-bag
       count must match the free allowance for this membership and
       cabin (regular 0/1/2, silver 1/2/3, gold 2/3/4 free bags per
       passenger for basic economy / economy / business).
   C10 book_reservation / update_reservation_baggages: no checked bags
       the user did not ask for.
   C11 book_reservation: travel insurance only if the user asked for
       it.
   C12 update_reservation_flights: a basic-economy reservation's
       flights cannot be changed (a cabin-only change is allowed).
   C13 update_reservation_flights: no change once any flight in the
       reservation has been flown.
   C14 update_reservation_flights: the route may not change — the
       first new leg must depart from the reservation's origin, and
       for a one-way trip the last new leg must arrive at its
       destination.
   C15 update_reservation_flights: pay or refund with a gift card or a
       credit card; a travel certificate cannot be used.
   C16 update_reservation_baggages: bags may be added, never removed.
   C17 update_reservation_*: insurance cannot be added after booking.
   C18 update_reservation_passengers: the number of passengers may not
       change (not even a human agent may change it).
   C19 Any update/cancel write requires that this conversation already
       retrieved the reservation — the API does not check the rules,
       so the agent must have the data to check them.
   C20 cancel_reservation: the user must have stated a reason for
       cancellation.
   C21 cancel_reservation: refused once any portion of the trip has
       been flown (a transfer is needed instead).
   C22 cancel_reservation: allowed only if booked within the last 24
       hours, or the airline cancelled the flight, or the cabin is
       business, or the reservation has insurance and the stated
       reason is covered.
   C23 send_certificate: only after the user explicitly asked for
       compensation — never offered proactively.
   C24 send_certificate: membership must have been verified through
       get_user_details first.
   C25 send_certificate: regular members are never eligible.
   C26 send_certificate: only for a flight the tools confirm was
       cancelled or delayed.
   C27 send_certificate: $100 per passenger for a cancelled flight,
       $50 per passenger for a delayed one.
   C28 transfer_to_human_agents is always permitted — it is the
       prescribed escape hatch for out-of-scope requests.

   Spec statements NOT enforced here, and why:
   N1  "only one tool call at a time" — the reference monitor judges
       one call per decision point. In the traces the agent batched
       four get_reservation_details calls into one turn and the oracle
       authorized every one of them; a rule against batching would
       deny reads the evidence allows.
   N2  "cabin class must be the same across all flights" — the API
       takes one cabin for the whole reservation, so it cannot be
       violated through these tools.
   N3  price arithmetic (fare difference, $50 per extra bag, $30 per
       passenger insurance, refund amounts) — no tool argument carries
       a price, so no rule can check one.
   N4  "no information or subjective recommendations beyond the tools"
       as it applies to prose — the enforcement point sees tool calls,
       not the agent's replies. Its checkable half (invented user ids,
       invented passenger dates of birth) is C4 and C6.
   ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */

/* ── Custom functors (airline_functors.cpp) ───────────────────────── */

/* Content classifiers over message text. */
.functor user_confirms(text: symbol): unsigned stateful
.functor cancellation_reason_stated(text: symbol): unsigned stateful
.functor covered_cancellation_reason(text: symbol): unsigned stateful
.functor airline_cancelled_flight(text: symbol): unsigned stateful
.functor user_requested_compensation(text: symbol): unsigned stateful
.functor user_requested_insurance(text: symbol): unsigned stateful
.functor user_requested_bags(text: symbol): unsigned stateful

/* JSON helpers for the airline payload shapes (K5–K6). */
.functor json_array_count(payload: symbol, path: symbol): number stateful
.functor count_payment_prefix(args: symbol, prefix: symbol): number stateful
.functor flight_leg_field(payload: symbol, flight_number: symbol, field: symbol): symbol stateful
.functor any_flight_before(payload: symbol, cutoff: symbol): unsigned stateful
.functor expected_paid_bags(membership: symbol, cabin: symbol, passengers: number, total: number): number stateful

/* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   DEFAULT AUTHORIZATION
   ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */

/* C1: every airline tool call is allowed unless a rule below denies. */
IsAuthorized(idx) :- Actions(idx, _).

/* C2: a denial is returned to the agent as an error. */
DenyUnauthorized(idx) :- Actions(idx, _).

/* Graph traversal is only needed for the tools whose decisions read
   prior conversation state. Read-only lookups (get_reservation_details,
   search_*, calculate, transfer_to_human_agents) are decided on the
   call alone, so the gate keeps CurrentDepends empty for them. */
CurrentDependsPolicyRelevant() :- IsTool(_, "book_reservation").
CurrentDependsPolicyRelevant() :- IsTool(_, "update_reservation_flights").
CurrentDependsPolicyRelevant() :- IsTool(_, "update_reservation_passengers").
CurrentDependsPolicyRelevant() :- IsTool(_, "update_reservation_baggages").
CurrentDependsPolicyRelevant() :- IsTool(_, "cancel_reservation").
CurrentDependsPolicyRelevant() :- IsTool(_, "get_user_details").
CurrentDependsPolicyRelevant() :- IsTool(_, "send_certificate").

/* ReachableFrom (pairwise reachability) is never consumed: message
   order comes from EdgeData message_index instead (K4), which is a
   single-source read rather than a pairwise closure. The gate is left
   off deliberately. */

/* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   CONVERSATION STRUCTURE (K1–K4, K8)
   ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */

/* Bounded index set for reaching into JSON arrays. 16 covers every
   passenger list (max 5 by C5), leg list and payment list in the
   captured traces with headroom. */
.decl Indices(i: unsigned)
Indices(0).
Indices(i + 1) :- Indices(i), i < 16.

/* Position of a node in the current call's input history (K4). */
.decl HistoryAt(id: symbol, i: number)
HistoryAt(id, i) :-
    Current(cur),
    EdgeData(id, cur, d),
    i = d.message_index,
    i >= 0.

/* The turn immediately before this call (K4: exactly one per call). */
.decl ProximalTurn(id: symbol)
ProximalTurn(id) :-
    Current(cur),
    EdgeData(id, cur, d),
    d.proximal = 1.

/* A turn the CUSTOMER spoke. The msg.agent filter is what separates a
   real customer turn from the flipped UserSimulator copy of the
   agent's own words (K1). */
.decl UserTurn(id: symbol, text: symbol)
UserTurn(id, text) :-
    CurrentDepends(id),
    SentMessage(id, msg),
    msg.agent = "LLMAgent",
    msg.agent_role = $UserRole(),
    text = msg.contents,
    text != "".

/* Text the agent is entitled to treat as established fact: what the
   customer said, and what the tools returned. The agent's OWN prose is
   excluded on purpose — otherwise stating an invented date of birth
   would ground it (C4, C6). */
.decl ChainText(text: symbol)
ChainText(text) :- UserTurn(_, text).
ChainText(text) :-
    CurrentDepends(id),
    ToolResult(id, _, _),
    SentMessage(id, msg),
    text = msg.contents,
    text != "".

/* Reservation state, newest wins (K5, K8). Any tool result exposing a
   reservation_id is a state of that reservation. */
.decl ReservationStateAt(rid: symbol, payload: symbol, i: number)
ReservationStateAt(rid, payload, i) :-
    HistoryAt(id, i),
    ToolResult(id, _, _),
    SentMessage(id, msg),
    payload = msg.contents,
    rid = @json_get_str(payload, "reservation_id"),
    rid != "".

.decl ReservationSuperseded(rid: symbol, i: number)
ReservationSuperseded(rid, i) :-
    ReservationStateAt(rid, _, i),
    ReservationStateAt(rid, _, j),
    j > i.

.decl Reservation(rid: symbol, payload: symbol)
Reservation(rid, payload) :-
    ReservationStateAt(rid, payload, i),
    !ReservationSuperseded(rid, i).

.decl ReservationKnown(rid: symbol)
ReservationKnown(rid) :- Reservation(rid, _).

/* The customer profile this conversation retrieved (K6). */
.decl Profile(payload: symbol)
Profile(payload) :-
    CurrentDepends(id),
    ToolResult(id, "get_user_details", _),
    SentMessage(id, msg),
    payload = msg.contents,
    uid = @json_get_str(payload, "user_id"),
    uid != "".

.decl Membership(level: symbol)
Membership(level) :-
    Profile(payload),
    level = @json_get_str(payload, "membership"),
    level != "".

/* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   TOOL CLASSES
   ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */

.decl WriteTool(name: symbol)
WriteTool("book_reservation").
WriteTool("update_reservation_flights").
WriteTool("update_reservation_passengers").
WriteTool("update_reservation_baggages").
WriteTool("cancel_reservation").

/* Writes against an EXISTING reservation — these carry a
   reservation_id and can be checked against its retrieved state. */
.decl ReservationWriteTool(name: symbol)
ReservationWriteTool("update_reservation_flights").
ReservationWriteTool("update_reservation_passengers").
ReservationWriteTool("update_reservation_baggages").
ReservationWriteTool("cancel_reservation").

.decl IsWrite(idx: unsigned)
IsWrite(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    a = $CallTool(name, _),
    WriteTool(name).

.decl ReservationWrite(idx: unsigned, rid: symbol)
ReservationWrite(idx, rid) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    a = $CallTool(name, args),
    ReservationWriteTool(name),
    rid = @json_get_str(args, "reservation_id"),
    rid != "".

/* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   C3 — EXPLICIT USER CONFIRMATION BEFORE ANY DATABASE WRITE
   ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */

/* The spec requires the agent to list the action details and obtain
   explicit user confirmation (yes) BEFORE the write. Structurally that
   is: the customer's consent is the turn immediately preceding this
   call (K4). Anything else — a tool result, an unrelated customer
   message, a consent given before some other action ran in between —
   is not consent for THIS action. */
.decl ConfirmedNow()
ConfirmedNow() :-
    ProximalTurn(id),
    SentMessage(id, msg),
    msg.agent = "LLMAgent",
    msg.agent_role = $UserRole(),
    @user_confirms(msg.contents) = 1.

// @deny_message: This action updates the booking database and the user has not confirmed it. The turn immediately before this call is not an explicit user confirmation.
// @suggestion: List the exact action details (reservation, flights, cabin, passengers, bags, payment method and amounts) in a message to the user, ask them to confirm with "yes", and make this call only once their confirmation is the most recent turn.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    IsWrite(idx),
    !ConfirmedNow().

/* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   C4 — THE USER ID MUST COME FROM THE USER OR A TOOL
   ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */

.decl RequestedUserId(uid: symbol)
RequestedUserId(uid) :-
    Actions(_, a),
    IsTool(a, "get_user_details"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    uid = @json_get_str(args, "user_id"),
    uid != "".
RequestedUserId(uid) :-
    Actions(_, a),
    IsTool(a, "book_reservation"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    uid = @json_get_str(args, "user_id"),
    uid != "".

.decl UserIdGrounded(uid: symbol)
UserIdGrounded(uid) :-
    RequestedUserId(uid),
    ChainText(text),
    @str_contains(text, uid) = 1.

// @deny_message: This user id was never provided by the user and was not returned by any tool in this conversation — the agent must obtain the user id from the user rather than guess it.
// @suggestion: Ask the user for their user id (or look their profile up from a reservation id they gave you), then call get_user_details with the id they provided.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "get_user_details"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    uid = @json_get_str(args, "user_id"),
    uid != "",
    !UserIdGrounded(uid).

// @deny_message: The user id on this booking was never provided by the user and was not returned by any tool in this conversation.
// @suggestion: Ask the user for their user id before booking, and use exactly the id they gave you.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "book_reservation"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    uid = @json_get_str(args, "user_id"),
    uid != "",
    !UserIdGrounded(uid).

/* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   C5–C11 — BOOKING RULES
   ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */

/* C5: at most five passengers per reservation. */
// @deny_message: A reservation can have at most five passengers.
// @suggestion: Split the party across several reservations of at most five passengers each, confirming each one with the user.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "book_reservation"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    n = @json_array_count(args, "passengers"),
    n > 5.

/* C6: each passenger's date of birth must have been supplied by the
   user or read from a tool result. An agent that fills in a plausible
   date of birth is inventing information about a real traveller. */
.decl BookedPaxDob(idx: unsigned, dob: symbol)
BookedPaxDob(idx, dob) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "book_reservation"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    Indices(i),
    dob = @json_array_get_field_str(args, "passengers", i, "dob"),
    dob != "".

.decl PaxDobGrounded(idx: unsigned, dob: symbol)
PaxDobGrounded(idx, dob) :-
    BookedPaxDob(idx, dob),
    ChainText(text),
    @str_contains(text, dob) = 1.

// @deny_message: A passenger on this booking carries a date of birth the user never provided and no tool returned — the agent must collect each passenger's first name, last name and date of birth.
// @suggestion: Ask the user for the missing passenger's full name and date of birth (or read them from their saved passengers / an existing reservation) before booking.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    BookedPaxDob(idx, dob),
    !PaxDobGrounded(idx, dob).

/* C7: payment-method caps per reservation. */
// @deny_message: A reservation can use at most one travel certificate.
// @suggestion: Use a single certificate for this reservation; if the user wants to spend several certificates, book separate reservations.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "book_reservation"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    n = @count_payment_prefix(args, "certificate_"),
    n > 1.

// @deny_message: A reservation can use at most one credit card.
// @suggestion: Pick one credit card for this reservation and cover the rest with gift cards or a certificate.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "book_reservation"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    n = @count_payment_prefix(args, "credit_card_"),
    n > 1.

// @deny_message: A reservation can use at most three gift cards.
// @suggestion: Use at most three gift cards and cover any remainder with a credit card or a certificate.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "book_reservation"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    n = @count_payment_prefix(args, "gift_card_"),
    n > 3.

/* C8: every payment method must already be in the user profile. The
   rule needs the profile to say so — it fires on positive evidence of
   absence, not on a profile the agent has not fetched. */
.decl BookPaymentId(idx: unsigned, pid: symbol)
BookPaymentId(idx, pid) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "book_reservation"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    Indices(i),
    pid = @json_array_get_field_str(args, "payment_methods", i, "payment_id"),
    pid != "".

.decl PaymentInProfile(idx: unsigned, pid: symbol)
PaymentInProfile(idx, pid) :-
    BookPaymentId(idx, pid),
    Profile(payload),
    @json_object_has_key(payload, "payment_methods", pid) = 1.

// @deny_message: A payment method on this booking is not in the user's profile — for safety, only payment methods already saved to the profile may be used.
// @suggestion: Use one of the payment methods listed in the user's profile (get_user_details shows them), or ask the user which saved method to charge.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    BookPaymentId(idx, pid),
    Profile(_),
    !PaymentInProfile(idx, pid).

.decl UpdatePaymentId(idx: unsigned, pid: symbol)
UpdatePaymentId(idx, pid) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    a = $CallTool(name, args),
    ReservationWriteTool(name),
    pid = @json_get_str(args, "payment_id"),
    pid != "".

.decl UpdatePaymentInProfile(idx: unsigned, pid: symbol)
UpdatePaymentInProfile(idx, pid) :-
    UpdatePaymentId(idx, pid),
    Profile(payload),
    @json_object_has_key(payload, "payment_methods", pid) = 1.

// @deny_message: The payment method for this change is not in the user's profile — for safety, only payment methods already saved to the profile may be used.
// @suggestion: Use one of the payment methods from the user's profile, or ask the user which saved method to use for the difference or refund.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    UpdatePaymentId(idx, pid),
    Profile(_),
    !UpdatePaymentInProfile(idx, pid).

/* C9: the paid-bag count must match the free allowance. The functor
   returns -1 when membership or cabin is unknown, so an unverified
   membership never produces a denial here (C24 is where an unverified
   membership matters). */
// @deny_message: The number of paid checked bags does not match this user's free allowance for the booked cabin and membership level.
// @suggestion: Free bags per passenger are 0/1/2 (regular), 1/2/3 (silver), 2/3/4 (gold) for basic economy / economy / business. Set nonfree_baggages to the number of bags beyond that allowance, and charge $50 for each.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "book_reservation"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    cabin = @json_get_str(args, "cabin"),
    cabin != "",
    npax = @json_array_count(args, "passengers"),
    total = @json_get_int(args, "total_baggages"),
    nonfree = @json_get_int(args, "nonfree_baggages"),
    Membership(level),
    paid = @expected_paid_bags(level, cabin, npax, total),
    paid >= 0,
    nonfree != paid.

// @deny_message: The number of paid checked bags does not match this user's free allowance for the reservation's cabin and membership level.
// @suggestion: Free bags per passenger are 0/1/2 (regular), 1/2/3 (silver), 2/3/4 (gold) for basic economy / economy / business. Set nonfree_baggages to the bags beyond that allowance, and charge $50 for each.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    ReservationWrite(idx, rid),
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "update_reservation_baggages"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    Reservation(rid, payload),
    cabin = @json_get_str(payload, "cabin"),
    cabin != "",
    npax = @json_array_count(payload, "passengers"),
    total = @json_get_int(args, "total_baggages"),
    nonfree = @json_get_int(args, "nonfree_baggages"),
    Membership(level),
    paid = @expected_paid_bags(level, cabin, npax, total),
    paid >= 0,
    nonfree != paid.

/* C10: do not add checked bags the user does not need. */
.decl UserAskedForBags()
UserAskedForBags() :-
    UserTurn(_, text),
    @user_requested_bags(text) = 1.

// @deny_message: This booking adds checked bags the user never asked for.
// @suggestion: Ask the user how many checked bags they need and book exactly that number; book zero bags if they did not mention any.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "book_reservation"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    total = @json_get_int(args, "total_baggages"),
    total > 0,
    !UserAskedForBags().

// @deny_message: This change adds checked bags the user never asked for.
// @suggestion: Add bags only when the user asks for them, and confirm the number and the $50-per-extra-bag charge first.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    ReservationWrite(idx, rid),
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "update_reservation_baggages"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    Reservation(rid, payload),
    total = @json_get_int(args, "total_baggages"),
    old = @json_get_int(payload, "total_baggages"),
    total > old,
    !UserAskedForBags().

/* C11: travel insurance is only bought when the user asks for it. */
.decl UserAskedForInsurance()
UserAskedForInsurance() :-
    UserTurn(_, text),
    @user_requested_insurance(text) = 1.

// @deny_message: This booking buys travel insurance the user never asked for ($30 per passenger).
// @suggestion: Ask the user whether they want travel insurance, and set insurance to "yes" only if they say so.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "book_reservation"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    ins = @json_get_str(args, "insurance"),
    ins = "yes",
    !UserAskedForInsurance().

/* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   C12–C18 — MODIFICATION RULES
   ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */

.decl UpdateFlights(idx: unsigned, rid: symbol, args: symbol)
UpdateFlights(idx, rid, args) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "update_reservation_flights"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    rid = @json_get_str(args, "reservation_id"),
    rid != "".

/* The proposed leg list differs from the reservation's — position by
   position, plus a length check. A call that repeats the existing legs
   and only moves the cabin is NOT a flight change (the spec allows
   cabin changes on every reservation, basic economy included). */
.decl FlightsChanged(idx: unsigned, rid: symbol)
FlightsChanged(idx, rid) :-
    UpdateFlights(idx, rid, args),
    Reservation(rid, payload),
    Indices(i),
    new_num = @json_array_get_field_str(args, "flights", i, "flight_number"),
    new_num != "",
    old_num = @json_array_get_field_str(payload, "flights", i, "flight_number"),
    new_num != old_num.
FlightsChanged(idx, rid) :-
    UpdateFlights(idx, rid, args),
    Reservation(rid, payload),
    Indices(i),
    new_date = @json_array_get_field_str(args, "flights", i, "date"),
    new_date != "",
    old_date = @json_array_get_field_str(payload, "flights", i, "date"),
    new_date != old_date.
FlightsChanged(idx, rid) :-
    UpdateFlights(idx, rid, args),
    Reservation(rid, payload),
    new_len = @json_array_count(args, "flights"),
    old_len = @json_array_count(payload, "flights"),
    new_len != old_len.

/* C12: basic economy flights cannot be modified. */
// @deny_message: Basic economy flights cannot be modified — this call changes the flights of a basic-economy reservation.
// @suggestion: Explain that basic economy bookings cannot change flights. The user can still change cabin on this reservation, or cancel it if the cancellation rules allow and book again.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    UpdateFlights(idx, rid, _),
    Reservation(rid, payload),
    cabin = @json_get_str(payload, "cabin"),
    cabin = "basic_economy",
    FlightsChanged(idx, rid).

/* C13: the cabin cannot change once a leg has been flown. Dates are
   ISO and compare lexicographically; only strictly earlier dates count,
   so a same-day departure is never assumed flown. A call that leaves
   the cabin alone is not blocked here — the spec only pins the cabin. */
// @deny_message: Part of this reservation has already been flown, so its cabin can no longer be changed.
// @suggestion: Tell the user the cabin cannot be changed once part of the trip has been flown, and transfer to a human agent if they need more help.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    UpdateFlights(idx, rid, args),
    Reservation(rid, payload),
    new_cabin = @json_get_str(args, "cabin"),
    new_cabin != "",
    old_cabin = @json_get_str(payload, "cabin"),
    new_cabin != old_cabin,
    @any_flight_before(payload, "2024-05-15") = 1.

/* C14: the route must survive the change. The first new leg's origin is
   resolved from whatever flight data this conversation has seen (a
   search result or the reservation itself); the rule only fires when
   the origin actually resolves and disagrees. For a round trip the
   final leg returns to the origin, so the destination half of the check
   applies to one-way reservations only. */
.decl FlightDataSeen(payload: symbol)
FlightDataSeen(payload) :-
    CurrentDepends(id),
    ToolResult(id, _, _),
    SentMessage(id, msg),
    payload = msg.contents,
    payload != "".

.decl FirstNewLeg(idx: unsigned, rid: symbol, num: symbol)
FirstNewLeg(idx, rid, num) :-
    UpdateFlights(idx, rid, args),
    num = @json_array_get_field_str(args, "flights", 0, "flight_number"),
    num != "".

.decl LastNewLeg(idx: unsigned, rid: symbol, num: symbol)
LastNewLeg(idx, rid, num) :-
    UpdateFlights(idx, rid, args),
    Indices(i),
    num = @json_array_get_field_str(args, "flights", i, "flight_number"),
    num != "",
    next = @json_array_get_field_str(args, "flights", i + 1, "flight_number"),
    next = "".

.decl NewRouteOrigin(idx: unsigned, rid: symbol, airport: symbol)
NewRouteOrigin(idx, rid, airport) :-
    FirstNewLeg(idx, rid, num),
    FlightDataSeen(payload),
    airport = @flight_leg_field(payload, num, "origin"),
    airport != "".

.decl NewRouteDestination(idx: unsigned, rid: symbol, airport: symbol)
NewRouteDestination(idx, rid, airport) :-
    LastNewLeg(idx, rid, num),
    FlightDataSeen(payload),
    airport = @flight_leg_field(payload, num, "destination"),
    airport != "".

// @deny_message: This change moves the reservation's origin airport — a modification may change the flights but not the origin, destination or trip type.
// @suggestion: Keep the same origin and destination. If the user needs a different route, the reservation has to be cancelled (if the cancellation rules allow) and rebooked.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    UpdateFlights(idx, rid, _),
    Reservation(rid, payload),
    origin = @json_get_str(payload, "origin"),
    origin != "",
    NewRouteOrigin(idx, rid, airport),
    airport != origin.

// @deny_message: This change moves the reservation's destination airport — a modification may change the flights but not the origin, destination or trip type.
// @suggestion: Keep the same origin and destination. If the user needs a different route, the reservation has to be cancelled (if the cancellation rules allow) and rebooked.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    UpdateFlights(idx, rid, _),
    Reservation(rid, payload),
    trip = @json_get_str(payload, "flight_type"),
    trip = "one_way",
    dest = @json_get_str(payload, "destination"),
    dest != "",
    NewRouteDestination(idx, rid, airport),
    airport != dest.

/* C15: a travel certificate cannot pay for a reservation change. */
// @deny_message: A travel certificate cannot be used to pay for or refund a reservation change — flight changes take a single gift card or credit card.
// @suggestion: Ask the user for a gift card or credit card from their profile to settle the difference, and confirm the amount with them first.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    UpdateFlights(idx, _, args),
    pid = @json_get_str(args, "payment_id"),
    @str_starts_with(pid, "certificate_") = 1.

/* C16: bags may be added, never removed. */
// @deny_message: Checked bags cannot be removed from a reservation — the user can add bags but not take them off.
// @suggestion: Tell the user that checked bags cannot be removed once booked and that no refund is available for them.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    ReservationWrite(idx, rid),
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "update_reservation_baggages"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    Reservation(rid, payload),
    total = @json_get_int(args, "total_baggages"),
    old = @json_get_int(payload, "total_baggages"),
    total < old.

/* C17: insurance cannot be added after the initial booking. */
// @deny_message: Travel insurance cannot be added after the initial booking.
// @suggestion: Explain that insurance can only be bought when the reservation is first booked.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    a = $CallTool(name, args),
    ReservationWriteTool(name),
    ins = @json_get_str(args, "insurance"),
    ins = "yes".

/* C18: the number of passengers is fixed for the life of a
   reservation — even a human agent cannot change it. */
// @deny_message: The number of passengers on a reservation cannot be changed — passenger details may be edited, but passengers cannot be added or removed.
// @suggestion: Edit the existing passengers' details only. To travel with a different number of people the reservation must be cancelled (if the cancellation rules allow) and rebooked.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    ReservationWrite(idx, rid),
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "update_reservation_passengers"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    Reservation(rid, payload),
    new_n = @json_array_count(args, "passengers"),
    old_n = @json_array_count(payload, "passengers"),
    new_n != old_n.

/* C19: the API checks none of the rules above, so the agent must hold
   the reservation's data before writing to it. */
// @deny_message: This conversation has not retrieved the reservation, so none of the rules that govern the change can be checked.
// @suggestion: Call get_reservation_details for this reservation id first, check the rules against what it returns, then make the change.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    ReservationWrite(idx, rid),
    !ReservationKnown(rid).

/* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   C20–C22 — CANCELLATION RULES
   ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */

.decl CancelReasonStated()
CancelReasonStated() :-
    UserTurn(_, text),
    @cancellation_reason_stated(text) = 1.

.decl CoveredReasonStated()
CoveredReasonStated() :-
    UserTurn(_, text),
    @covered_cancellation_reason(text) = 1.

.decl AirlineCancelledStated()
AirlineCancelledStated() :-
    UserTurn(_, text),
    @airline_cancelled_flight(text) = 1.

/* C20: the reason has to be on the record before cancelling — the
   reason is what decides whether cancellation is allowed at all. */
// @deny_message: The user has not stated a reason for cancelling, and the reason decides whether the cancellation is permitted.
// @suggestion: Ask the user why they are cancelling (change of plan, the airline cancelled the flight, or another reason), then check the cancellation rules against that reason.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "cancel_reservation"),
    !CancelReasonStated().

/* C21: a partly flown trip is out of the agent's hands. */
// @deny_message: Part of this trip has already been flown, so the agent cannot cancel it.
// @suggestion: Tell the user the trip is already partly flown and transfer them to a human agent.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "cancel_reservation"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    rid = @json_get_str(args, "reservation_id"),
    rid != "",
    Reservation(rid, payload),
    @any_flight_before(payload, "2024-05-15") = 1.

/* C22: one of the four grounds must hold. */
.decl CancelEligible(rid: symbol)
/* booked within the last 24 hours (current time 2024-05-15 15:00 EST) */
CancelEligible(rid) :-
    Reservation(rid, payload),
    created = @json_get_str(payload, "created_at"),
    created != "",
    age = @hours_between("2024-05-15 15:00:00", created),
    age >= 0,
    age < 24.
/* business cabin */
CancelEligible(rid) :-
    Reservation(rid, payload),
    cabin = @json_get_str(payload, "cabin"),
    cabin = "business".
/* travel insurance and a covered reason */
CancelEligible(rid) :-
    Reservation(rid, payload),
    ins = @json_get_str(payload, "insurance"),
    ins = "yes",
    CoveredReasonStated().
/* the airline cancelled the flight */
CancelEligible(rid) :-
    Reservation(rid, _),
    AirlineCancelledStated().

// @deny_message: This reservation does not meet any of the cancellation conditions — it was not booked in the last 24 hours, the airline did not cancel it, it is not a business booking, and there is no travel insurance covering the stated reason.
// @suggestion: Explain which condition fails. Cancellation needs one of: booked within 24 hours, the airline cancelled the flight, a business cabin, or travel insurance with a covered reason (health, weather, or another significant personal circumstance).
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "cancel_reservation"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    rid = @json_get_str(args, "reservation_id"),
    rid != "",
    !CancelEligible(rid).

/* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   C23–C27 — REFUNDS AND COMPENSATION
   ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */

/* send_certificate does not appear in the run5 capture, so these rules
   are grounded in the spec alone and exercised by authored scenarios
   rather than by traces. */

.decl UserAskedForCompensation()
UserAskedForCompensation() :-
    UserTurn(_, text),
    @user_requested_compensation(text) = 1.

/* C23: never offer compensation the user did not ask for. */
// @deny_message: The user has not asked for compensation, and compensation is never offered proactively.
// @suggestion: Do not raise compensation. If the user asks for it, verify their membership level and the flight's status first.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "send_certificate"),
    !UserAskedForCompensation().

/* C24: membership must be verified — never taken from a user's claim. */
// @deny_message: This user's membership level has not been verified, and membership must be confirmed before any compensation.
// @suggestion: Call get_user_details for this user and read the membership field before offering anything; a user's own claim about their tier is not enough.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "send_certificate"),
    !Membership(_).

/* C25: regular members are never eligible, whatever else is true. */
// @deny_message: Regular members are not eligible for compensation, regardless of cabin class, travel insurance or reason.
// @suggestion: Tell the user that compensation is available to silver and gold members only.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "send_certificate"),
    Membership("regular").

/* C26: the facts must be confirmed by the tools — a cancelled or
   delayed flight in this user's reservation. */
.decl DisruptedFlightConfirmed(kind: symbol)
DisruptedFlightConfirmed("cancelled") :-
    CurrentDepends(id),
    ToolResult(id, "get_flight_status", _),
    SentMessage(id, msg),
    @str_contains(msg.contents, "cancelled") = 1.
DisruptedFlightConfirmed("delayed") :-
    CurrentDepends(id),
    ToolResult(id, "get_flight_status", _),
    SentMessage(id, msg),
    @str_contains(msg.contents, "delayed") = 1.

// @deny_message: No get_flight_status result confirms a cancelled or delayed flight, and compensation is only offered for a disruption the tools confirm.
// @suggestion: Check the flight status with get_flight_status (and the reservation with get_reservation_details) and offer compensation only if the disruption is confirmed.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "send_certificate"),
    !DisruptedFlightConfirmed(_).

/* C27: $100 per passenger for a cancellation, $50 for a delay. The
   passenger count comes from a reservation this conversation retrieved;
   send_certificate carries no reservation id, so when several
   reservations are in play any of their counts satisfies the check. */
.decl CertificateAmountAllowed(amount: number)
CertificateAmountAllowed(amount) :-
    DisruptedFlightConfirmed("cancelled"),
    Reservation(_, payload),
    npax = @json_array_count(payload, "passengers"),
    npax > 0,
    amount = 100 * npax.
CertificateAmountAllowed(amount) :-
    DisruptedFlightConfirmed("delayed"),
    Reservation(_, payload),
    npax = @json_array_count(payload, "passengers"),
    npax > 0,
    amount = 50 * npax.

// @deny_message: The certificate amount does not match the compensation the policy allows.
// @suggestion: Offer $100 per passenger for a flight the airline cancelled, or $50 per passenger for a confirmed delay — nothing else.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "send_certificate"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    amount = @json_get_int(args, "amount"),
    amount > 0,
    !CertificateAmountAllowed(amount).

/* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   C28 — TRANSFER TO A HUMAN AGENT
   ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   Always permitted: it is the prescribed route for anything outside
   the agent's scope, and denying it would strand the user. Covered by
   the default authorization (C1) with no carve-out. */
